# Per-target clones never live in this tree -- they live under $FACTORY_TREES (H-0406) -- and a tick
# run in-tree during development must not dirty it. H-0407 then moved the supervisor's state box HERE,
# beside the code that writes it, so the live journal, ledger, lock and halt are the four rules at the
# foot of this file rather than a directory somewhere else:
.factory-run/
.factory-ledger.json
.factory-log/
.factory-claims/
.factory-timers/
.factory-mutate/
.factory-mutation-journal.jsonl
.factory-mutation-state.json
.factory-mutation-v1.json
.factory-audit-remote.json
.factory-sealed-history.jsonl
.factory-watchdog-journal.jsonl
.factory-watchdog-state.json
.factory-watchdog-alerts.json

# Selftest fixtures and the --self-test legs' scratch output.
/check-close-verb.*.selftest.log
/check-decisions.*.selftest.log
/check-denies.*.selftest.log
/check-doc-labels.*.selftest.log
/check-scripts.*.selftest.log
/check-mutation-*.selftest.json
/mutate-report.*.selftest.json
/mutation-variants.*.selftest.tsv
*.tmp

# Inherited hygiene: this tree was once parental-lockout's, and its built
# binary is the four-times-committed 10 MB blob (memory #1264). The rule
# travels so a stray `go build` can never be swept in by `git add -A` here.
/plock
/plock.exe
/bin/
*.exe

# scanner bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The delivery supervisor's own state, which H-0407 put beside the harness rather than in a state
# directory of its own. All four are machine state and none of them may read as dirt: measured 26 Nov
# on the first pass after the re-arm -- `SUPERVISOR-AT 3fafef6 dirty=1378`, then
# `MAIN-CHECKOUT-REFUSED cause=not-restorable shapes=untracked` and `SUPERVISOR-FF-REFUSED
# not-this-pass`, the supervisor's own hygiene gate refusing to fast-forward the tree the unit execs
# because the journal that pass had just written counted as untracked work. The product tree the box
# moved OUT of already ignored all four (its `.gitignore:65-68`); the harness took the box and not the
# rules. `HALT` is ignored for a second reason (#216): a halt one machine wrote must never be shipped
# to another by a commit.
/factory/log/
/factory/ledger/
/factory/run/
/factory/HALT
